{"id": "live-395", "title": "Kaanapali Land Management Corp. v. Newport Hospital Corporation (Maui Infrastructure Contribution Lien Foreclosure)", "category": "lending-foreclosure", "status": "pending", "date": "2026-09-29", "jurisdiction": "Circuit Court of the Second Circuit, State of Hawaii", "state": "HI", "amount": "Receivable and accrued interest under a 2014 Infrastructure Improvement Agreement capping KLMC's own contribution at up to $0.6 million; exact amount owed by NHC not disclosed", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1230058/000107997326001461/kaa10q-926final.htm", "summary": "Kaanapali Land, LLC disclosed in a November 12, 2026 Form 10-Q that its subsidiary, Kaanapali Land Management Corp. (KLMC), filed a foreclosure complaint in Maui on September 29, 2026 against Newport Hospital Corporation (NHC) after NHC failed to pay a receivable owed under a 2014 Infrastructure Improvement Agreement tied to KLMC's sale of roughly 14.9 acres in West Maui to NHC. NHC moved to stay or dismiss the foreclosure proceeding on November 5, 2026, and the company cautions there is no assurance KLMC will prevail or collect what it is owed.", "significance": "Shows how an infrastructure-cost-sharing obligation attached to a land sale can resurface a decade later as contested foreclosure litigation once a buyer disputes its contribution, and illustrates the added complexity when the disputed parcel sits inside a larger master-planned development where the seller has retained ongoing design and use-approval rights.", "judge": null, "tags": ["foreclosure", "land-development", "hawaii", "infrastructure-lien", "master-development"]}
